WEBVTT

00:00:02.500 --> 00:00:05.557
If your team ends the shift with sore shoulders or backs,

00:00:05.557 --> 00:00:08.668
look at the bench height before you look at anything else.

00:00:09.268 --> 00:00:12.010
Most plants use one bench height for every task.

00:00:12.290 --> 00:00:17.259
But soldering while seated and sealing cartons while standing need very different heights.

00:00:17.859 --> 00:00:26.374
As a guide, seated work such as labelling, soldering and documentation suits 750 to 850 millimetres.

00:00:26.654 --> 00:00:34.059
Standing work such as carton sealing, weighing and heavy assembly suits 900 to 1100 millimetres.

00:00:34.339 --> 00:00:37.167
The aim is relaxed shoulders and a neutral back.

00:00:37.447 --> 00:00:42.324
Adjust first for the task, then fine-tune for the operator using the station most.

00:00:42.924 --> 00:00:47.130
Furnisys Base benches adjust with leg extenders in 2 inch steps.

00:00:47.410 --> 00:00:49.348
Scitec adjusts in 1 inch steps.

00:00:49.628 --> 00:00:56.655
Pro comes in six heights from 700 to 1000 millimetres, and Flexi worktops move in 3 inch steps.

00:00:57.255 --> 00:00:59.845
Set the height for the task, then for the person.

00:01:00.125 --> 00:01:01.574
What is your bench height today?

00:01:01.854 --> 00:01:05.636
Measure it and comment below, and next, learn about reach zones.

00:01:06.236 --> 00:01:10.481
Furnisys: complete workspace systems, planned around your process.

